IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ma-s04-saving`

-- Tests for ma-s04-saving.l4.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 4 before the run:
-- "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to any misrepresentation or contract of sale made before 12 November 1993 except in so far
-- as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date."

§ `Tests -- s 4, the day before which it looks`

-- Strictly before 12 November 1993: the day before is before, the day itself is not.
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 13 11 1993)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 31 12 1992)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 1 1 1967)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4, "any misrepresentation or contract of sale made before 12 November 1993"`

-- Arguments: date the misrepresentation was made; the contract is a contract of sale; date the contract was made.
-- The misrepresentation was made before: that limb alone is enough.
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 20 11 1993)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The contract of sale was made before, the misrepresentation date not given: the second limb.
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The contract is not a contract of sale, though made before: that limb does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both made on or after the day: neither limb.
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 1 6 2020)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Facts not given: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4, "Nothing in this Act applies"`

-- Arguments: date the misrepresentation was made; the contract is a contract of sale; date the contract was made;
-- it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909.
-- Made before 12 November 1993 and not within the exception: nothing in the Act applies.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Contract of sale made before, misrepresentation date not given, not within the exception.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Within the exception: section 4 does not bar the Act.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made on the day itself or after: "made before 12 November 1993" is a date the text fixes in its own words, so section 4 does not bar the Act, JUST FALSE.
-- The day itself is not "before" it.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 1 6 2020)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 1 6 2020)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same when the contract is not a contract of sale: neither limb reaches it.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 1 1990)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The misrepresentation date is not given and the contract of sale was made on the day itself: the second limb does not reach it either, but the first limb is not decided, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 12 11 1993)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The exception is not known: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 11 11 1993)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The dates are not known: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
